//! The A4-shaped ASSUME-GUARANTEE activation for `infer_type`, over an
//! ABSTRACT module, with the two callee contracts as premises.
//!
//! Every declaration here is its own registration so that a kernel refusal
//! names the term that failed rather than the batch. The statements are the
//! ones `plan_how_it_closes_link4.txt` fixes, adjusted only where a hand
//! reduction of the machine showed the plan wrong -- each such change is
//! recorded in the declaration description that carries it.

use super::{SpecError, Specification};

