const DECLS: &[(&str, &str)] = &[
    (SRC_IR_OPT_SLOT_SOME, "The some-discriminator on an optional memory cell, as a Bool. The stage has no Or/And/False, so constructor disjointness (none is not some _) is expressed the only way this vocabulary allows: a Bool-valued function that computes to false on none and true on some, so none = some s becomes false = true by ir_eq_cong and is refuted by ir_bool_false_ne_true. Same shape as ir_load_slot. The pre-existing ir_option_is_some is IROption Nat only, which is why a monomorphic twin at IRMemSlot is needed. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_OPT_SLOT_SET_VAL, "Overwrite the VALUE of an optional cell, keeping its address and live bit (none stays none). It exists for constructor injectivity without Or/And: applied by ir_eq_cong to some (mk i old lv) = some (mk a v0 live) it yields some (mk i v lv) = some (mk a v live) in one step, so the address and live-bit equalities are carried THROUGH the equation rather than extracted from it -- no projection lemma and no ir_nat_eqb_sound. Value argument first so ir_opt_slot_set_val v is the A -> B a congruence takes (the ir_borrow_slot a precedent, eval_ir_lzd_fresh.rs). DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_MEM_LOOKUP_UPDATE_HIT, "*** THE HIT TWIN OF ir_mem_lookup_update_skip. *** A store to an address a lookup already resolves to cell (a, v0, live) makes the SAME lookup resolve to (a, v, live): address and live bit survive, only the contents change. Induction on the heap with the hypothesis generalised in the motive; at each cell a convoy on the machine's own ir_nat_eqb i a. Empty heap contradicts the hypothesis (none = some _, refuted through ir_opt_slot_some); a cell the update SKIPS the lookup skips too, so the IH carries; the cell the update HITS is the first cell the lookup hits, so the hypothesis names exactly that cell and ir_opt_slot_set_val rewrites its contents on both sides at once. _skip says a store disturbs no OTHER address; this says what it does at ITS address, which is what a load after a store through the same pointer reads back. It is what lets the Result slot sit ANYWHERE in memory (a real tick_heartbeat allocates, so after call 1 the slot is no longer at the head). Argument order is (mem, a, v0, v, live, h) -- the VALUE before the live bit. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_OPT_FUNC_IS_SOME, "Bool discriminator on IROption IRFunc (none -> false, some -> true), so a none = some g hypothesis on a FUNCTION lookup becomes Eq Bool Bool.false Bool.true by ir_eq_cong and is refuted by ir_bool_false_ne_true. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_OPT_GLOBAL_IS_SOME, "Bool discriminator on IROption IRGlobal, the IRGlobal twin of ir_opt_func_is_some. Used by ir_it_hg_nil to refute a hit in the EMPTY global table. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ENTRY, "infer_type's ENTRY machine, the one ir_init builds: function 0, block 0, pc 0, the two pointer parameters bound positionally, return destinations ds, caller stack rest, heap mem, counter na. Named rather than re-spelled at every use for the reason ir_it_dispatch_end and ir_it3_smach are: a multi-frame configuration written out four times is exactly the term that is wrong by one binding and fails an hour later. At ds := nil and rest := nil it is ir_it_mach0, the machine ir_it_init_is_mach0 pins. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ALLOCA_M, "The machine after b0 node 0, the alloca: block 0 pc 1 sitting ON the heartbeat call, %2 := IRScalar.ptr_ na (a PLAIN pointer, the counter as it stood at entry) in front of the two parameters, one LIVE undef cell at address na consed onto the head of memory, counter Nat.succ na. Locals in the reduced cons form ir_bind_params computes to. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_PUSH1_M, "The machine the instant tick_heartbeat's frame is pushed: callee frame (ir_func_id g1) (ir_func_entry g1) pc 0, parameters bound to the single argument ir_vl1 (ptr_ p), dests the call node's declared result [3]; beneath it the caller frame ADVANCED past the call, which is ir_it_dframe <post-alloca locals> ds; heap and counter the alloca's. This is VERBATIM hc1's premise configuration at d := ir_nl1 ir_d3 and r := ir_it_dframe loc ds :: rest, so hc1 splices in with one delta of this name and no rewriting. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_HB_RET, "What hc1 delivers: ir_ret_to with dests [3] into the b0 pc-2 caller frame over rest, at the heartbeat's final heap mem1 and counter na1, returning [ir_it_hb_answer sp]. It is VERBATIM ir_it_dispatch_seg's start configuration at loc := the post-alloca locals, which is what that seam was written for. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_PUSH2_M, "The machine the instant infer_type_fast's frame is pushed: callee frame (ir_func_id g2) (ir_func_entry g2) pc 0, parameters bound positionally to ir_vl2 (ptr_ p) (ptr_ q), dests [29]; beneath it the b5 caller frame advanced to pc ir_d1 carrying %4 := int_ 0 and %3 := the heartbeat answer over the post-alloca locals, dests ds; heap mem1 and counter na1 unchanged by the push. VERBATIM hc2's premise configuration at d := ir_nl1 ir_d29. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_FAST_RET, "What hc2 delivers: ir_ret_to with dests [29] into the advanced b5 caller frame over rest, at the inference's final heap mem2 and counter na2, returning [aggv spv]. ir_it_ag_hc2_lands_on_smach is the kernel-checked equation that this IS IRConfig.running (ir_it3_smach ...), where the transport seam starts. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL_K, "The call step with its callee LOOKUP SUSPENDED -- ir_call_exec's own body with the IROption last, the ir_lzm_after_load / ir_ite_after_store_lookup idiom applied to the MODULE axis. At an abstract module ir_call_exec (IRModule.mk fs gs) s rs fid args is stuck at the neutral ir_func_find fs fid; naming the continuation lets an Eq.subst over a callee premise rewrite that one occurrence and then compute. Generic in machine, result ids and argument ids, so ONE wrapper serves both calls: call 1 at rs := ir_nl1 ir_d3, args := ir_nl1 ir_d0 and call 2 at rs := ir_nl1 ir_d29, args := ir_nl2 ir_d0 ir_d1. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL_K_IS_CALL_EXEC, "Vacuity pin: ir_call_exec at ANY module, machine, result-id list, callee id and argument list IS ir_it_ag_call_k applied to that module's own function lookup, by delta alone (no iota -- the major stays neutral on both sides). Registered so the wrapper cannot drift from the machine's call arm; an undeclared id in a TYPE becomes a silent free variable, so a wrapper that only LOOKED like the arm would still elaborate. It covers call 2 as well as call 1, which is why this stage registers no second wrapper. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_STEP_ALLOCA, "infer_type's FIRST node -- %2 = alloca struct.2 -- at an ABSTRACT module, given only h0. One suspended-lookup Eq.subst on the fetch (ir_step unfolds to ir_step_f ... (ir_func_find fs ir_d0) at a cons-headed frame list, the ir_step_cons_fetch measurement), then Eq.refl: ir_alloca_exec at count none is ir_alloca_k with k = 1, binding %2 := IRScalar.ptr_ na (plain, not fat), consing one LIVE undef cell at Nat.add na 0 = na onto the head of memory and advancing the counter to Nat.add na 1 = Nat.succ na (Nat.add recurses on its SECOND argument; the same two reductions ir_lzd_dstep40 relies on at an abstract counter), pc 0 -> 1. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL1_FETCHED, "SHAPE pin, the ir_lzm_step_load idiom on the module axis: once the fetch of function 0 is resolved, executing b0 node 1 at the post-alloca machine IS ir_it_ag_call_k at the neutral ir_func_find fs ir_d1, by Eq.refl. Pins by computation that the node fetched at pc 1 is %3 = call fn1(%0) (ir_nodes_get walks one Nat.rec layer), that its declared results are [3] and its argument list [0], and that the one argument resolves head-first past %2 (ir_nat_eqb 2 0 = false) to ptr_ p. It is the exact term the call-step lemma's inner Eq.subst motive abstracts. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_STEP_CALL, "infer_type's SECOND node -- %3 = call fn1(%0), the tick_heartbeat call -- at an ABSTRACT module, given h0 (the fetch) and h1 (the callee). RE-DERIVED 2026-09-24 through the GENERIC call step ir_call_push (eval_ir_stack_split.rs), statement unchanged: the frame is the post-alloca frame at pc 1, the function and callee lookups are h0 and h1, and the block and node lookups are Eq.refl because ir_it_func is concrete (block 0 is ir_it_b0, node 1 its `call 1 [0]` with result id 3). The result ir_push is DEFINITIONALLY running (ir_it_ag_push1_m ..): the caller frame beneath the push is advanced past the call to pc 2, which is ir_it_dframe <post-alloca locals> ds after one delta on ir_it_dframe and one on ir_d2, and the declared type is checked against it. Heap and counter untouched by the push. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_PROLOGUE, "*** infer_type's first TWO steps at an ABSTRACT module. *** From the entry machine ir_init builds, two steps of IRModule.mk fs gs -- given only h0 (function 0 is the minted ir_it_func) and h1 (function 1 is SOME g1, otherwise unconstrained) -- reach ir_it_ag_push1_m, where g1's frame has just been pushed. Cost ir_d2 is DERIVED: b0 node 0 (alloca) then node 1 (the call push); the br b1 at node 2 is the caller's next node and is what the return resumes into. Proof: ir_steps ir_d2 peels definitionally to ir_steps ir_d1 after one ir_step (ir_drive_v1's succ/running arm), that step is ir_it_ag_step_alloca transported by ir_eq_cong, and ir_steps ir_d1 of a running machine is one ir_step, which is ir_it_ag_step_call. Module-generic: nothing here consults ir_it_module. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_SINGLETON_FIND, "The ONE reduction ir_it_hf_of_h0 turns on, pinned on its own so a refusal is attributable. Looking a function id up in the one-element table ir_it_module declares IS the stuck Bool.rec on the machine's own comparison of ir_it_func's id against the key: delta on ir_func_find, IRList.rec iota on the cons, delta on the CONSTANT ir_it_func to expose IRFunc.mk, IRFunc.rec iota binding i := ir_d0, leaving Bool.rec _ none (some ir_it_func) (ir_nat_eqb ir_d0 kf) -- stuck, because ir_nat_eqb ir_d0 kf whnfs to ir_nat_iszero kf at a neutral kf. The true minor carries the CONSTANT ir_it_func, not its unfolding, which is what lets h0 be transported along the hit in one iota. This is the step the ir_mem_lookup_update_skip template never had to take: its convoy major is a constructor-applied VARIABLE, this one needs a constant delta first. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_HF_OF_H0, "The function-table INCLUSION ir_mext_run needs, from the single hypothesis h0. ir_func_find (cons ir_it_func nil) kf unfolds (ir_it_singleton_find pins exactly this) to Bool.rec _ none (some ir_it_func) (ir_nat_eqb ir_d0 kf); a Bool equation convoy on that comparison splits it. FALSE: the hit is none = some gf, refuted through ir_opt_func_is_some and ir_bool_false_ne_true. TRUE: ir_nat_eqb_sound turns the machine's own test into ir_d0 = kf, and h0 is transported twice by Eq.subst -- first its right side from some ir_it_func (the Bool.rec at true, one iota) to some gf, then its key from ir_d0 to kf. No projection and no injectivity lemma. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_HG_NIL, "The global-table inclusion ir_mext_run needs when the source module has NO globals (ir_it_module's second field is IRList.nil IRGlobal), for an arbitrary target table gs. Vacuous: ir_global_find nil kg computes to none (IRList.rec on nil, so the neutral kg does not block), the premise is none = some gg, ir_opt_global_is_some turns it into false = true and ir_bool_false_ne_true closes it. Takes gs as an explicit binder before the forall so ir_it_hg_nil gs has exactly ir_mext_run's hg type. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_SEAM_EXT, "*** THE MODULE-EXTENSION TRANSPORT FOR infer_type. *** Any k-step run at the CONCRETE ir_it_module that ends RUNNING holds verbatim at the ABSTRACT IRModule.mk fs gs, given only h0. It is ir_mext_run at fs0 := cons ir_it_func nil, gs0 := nil, with the two inclusions; ir_it_module is definitionally that IRModule.mk (generated/ir_it.defs.txt), which is the ONE delta this declaration asks of the checker and the only place in the stage where it is asked. Every seam proved by Eq.refl at ir_it_module -- ir_it_dispatch_seg, ir_it_transport3_at -- is lifted by this one function with no re-proof. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_SEAM3_EXT, "ir_it_seam_ext at k := ir_d3, the step count of BOTH three-step seams (the dispatch seam br/extractfield/switch and the store/br/load transport). Stated over an abstract configuration and machine so it composes with either without any coordination on binders. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_DISPATCH_SEG_EXT, "infer_type's dispatch seam (br / extractfield / switch -- three steps from tick_heartbeat's return into b0 pc 2 to sitting ON call 2 in b5) at the ABSTRACT module, under h0 alone. ir_it_dispatch_seg proved it by Eq.refl at ir_it_module; ir_it_seam3_ext carries it across, and the h argument is SYNTACTICALLY ir_it_dispatch_seg's declared type so no defeq is asked here at all. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_LOC_FROM_ALLOCA, "COORDINATION PIN for loc: the frame ir_alloca_k builds at b0 pc 0 -- ir_frame_bind of the ENTRY frame at result id %2 with IRScalar.ptr_ na, na the counter BEFORE the alloca -- IS the block-0 pc-1 frame whose locals are the explicit three-binding list. That list is the loc every ir_it_ag_ statement is stated at: it is the only loc under which call 2's arguments %0/%1 can be READ (ir_binding_lookup walks past %4 and %3 into loc and is stuck at an abstract tail). The pointer is ptr_ na with the ENTRY counter, which is why hslot looks up address na. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL2_ARGS, "THE MEASUREMENT the call-2 piece turns on: at the dispatch-end machine over the CONCRETE post-alloca loc, resolving call 2's operands [%0, %1] computes to ir_vl2 (ptr_ p) (ptr_ q). ir_binding_lookup walks head-first -- for %0: %4, %3, %2 miss then %0 hits; for %1: 4, 3, 2, 0 miss then %1 hits -- nine closed-literal ir_nat_eqb decisions, none of which fires at an abstract loc. The payload spine sp is never forced. Registered on its own so that if the lookup computation is the wall, it is named here and not inside the push lemma. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL2_FETCHED, "The shape witness AFTER the fetch has been resolved: once the head frame's function lookup is some ir_it_func, ir_step_f at block 5 pc 0 computes through ir_block_find (five closed ir_nat_eqb misses b0..b4, then b5 hits), ir_nodes_get at pc 0 (the call fn2(%0,%1) -> %29 node), ir_exec_node, ir_exec's call arm and ir_call_exec's delta, arriving at ir_it_ag_call_k with the CALLEE lookup still neutral, by Eq.refl. This is the abstract-module counterpart of ir_it_dispatch_ends_at_the_call, which at ir_it_module computes that same lookup to none and halts. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL2_IS_PUSH, "Vacuity pin: ir_push at the dispatch-end machine with dests [29], callee g2 and the resolved arguments IS ir_it_ag_push2_m -- head frame (ir_func_id g2) (ir_func_entry g2) pc 0, locals ir_bind_params (ir_func_params g2) (ir_vl2 (ptr_ p) (ptr_ q)) nil, dests [29], over the ADVANCED caller frame at b5 pc ir_d1 (ir_frame_advance's Nat.succ Nat.zero) with the same locals and dests ds, over rest; heap mem1 and counter na1 untouched. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL2, "*** INFER_TYPE'S CALL-2 PUSH AT AN ABSTRACT MODULE. *** One ir_step from the dispatch seam's endpoint -- b5 pc 0, sitting ON call fn2(%0,%1) -> %29, locals %4 := int_ 0 and %3 := the heartbeat answer over the concrete post-alloca loc -- given only h0 and h2, IS the machine with g2's entry frame pushed (ir_it_ag_push2_m), VERBATIM the frame hc2 quantifies at d := ir_nl1 ir_d29. Proof: the suspended-lookup idiom twice -- Eq.subst h0 (symm) on the FETCH through ir_step_cons_fetch, then Eq.subst h2 (symm) on the CALLEE lookup inside ir_call_exec via the generic wrapper ir_it_ag_call_k at rs := [29], args := [0, 1] -- then Eq.refl, since with both options constructor-headed the fetch, the block/node lookups, the operand resolution and ir_push all compute. Nothing here names the callee's body: g2 is abstract, which is what makes hc2 a premise rather than a model. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CALL2_STEPS1, "The splice-ready form of ir_it_ag_call2: the same fact stated through the ITERATOR, which is what the ir_d4 = ir_d3 + ir_d1 split of the dispatch segment hands the assembly once the three-step seam has been rewritten inside it. Body unchanged; the declared type differs by exactly the reduction ir_it_ag_steps1_is_step pins, so a refusal is attributable to that reduction and not to the call step. Every other segment in the assembly is delivered in ir_steps form; without this twin the bridge would be an unnamed defeq inside the assembly's Eq.trans. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RESUME, "THE SPLICE after hc2, at an ARBITRARY locals list. The configuration hc2 delivers IS, by computation (ir_ret_to's cons arm then ir_frame_set_many's match), the RUNNING machine whose head frame is that same b5 frame with %29 bound to aggv spv on top of loc through ir_bind_params, pc still ir_d1 (a return does not advance -- the push already did), dests ds, over rest. Stated for an arbitrary loc because ir_ret_to never reads locals; ir_it_ag_hc2_lands_on_smach is the same fact at the CONCRETE loc the assembly is at, landing directly on ir_it3_smach. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RESUME_LOCALS, "The resumed frame's locals in explicit form: ir_bind_params [29] [aggv spv] loc is cons (%29, aggv spv) loc by computation, for every loc (the recursion is on the two concrete lists; loc is the nil-minor's value and is never inspected). This is the half of the hc2 splice that turns the machine's own spelling into the head-cons spelling ir_it3_loc5 is written in. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_LOC0, "infer_type's locals the instant b0's alloca has bound %2: the entry parameters %0 := ptr p and %1 := ptr q with %2 := ptr a on top, a the address ir_alloca_k minted (the entry counter). Written in the reduced cons form the kernel computes to, so it is definitionally the frame the prologue produces whatever spelling the prologue chose. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_LOC5, "The b5 frame's locals the instant call 2 has returned: %29 := aggv spv over %4 := int 0 and %3 := the heartbeat answer over ir_it3_loc0. This is the REAL shape, not ir_ite_loc: %2 sits FOURTH, under three literal ids, and every lookup of it walks past ir_nat_eqb 29 2, 4 2 and 3 2 (closed literals, all false) before ir_nat_eqb 2 2 hits, so the walk computes without any binding being rebound at the head. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_SMACH, "The machine the instant call 2 has returned into infer_type: function 0, block b5, pc 1 (ir_push advanced the caller's pc past the call node; ir_frame_set_many kept it), the store as the next node, the b5 locals of ir_it3_loc5, an ARBITRARY heap mem2 and counter na2. ir_it_ag_hc2_lands_on_smach is the kernel-checked equation saying this IS what hc2 delivers. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_AMACH, "The machine after the store: b5 pc 2 (ir_frame_advance), same locals, and the heap is ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv) -- a NEUTRAL term that is carried rather than computed, since nothing between the store and the load inspects memory. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_BMACH, "The machine after the br: block b3 pc zero (ir_frame_goto), locals unchanged because b3 declares no block parameters (ir_bind_params ir_nl0 nil loc = loc), the updated heap carried. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_LMACH, "The machine after the load: b3 pc 1 sitting ON the ret node (NOT executed here -- that is what lets ir_it_seam3_ext carry the seam to IRModule.mk fs gs and ir_it_ag_ret_loc finish it), with %5 := aggv spv bound on top. The load of an aggregate cell yields the cell's VALUE ITSELF (ir_load_cell -> ir_load_value (aggv spv)), no copy and no byte view: ir_load_view sees ir_mod_encs (IRModule.mk fs gs) = nil and is the identity, so ir_it_tresult is dropped. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_AFTER_STORE_LOOKUP, "The store with its liveness lookup SUSPENDED as a parameter -- ir_ite_after_store_lookup's shape with the slot abstract. At an abstract heap ir_mem_lookup mem2 a is stuck at a neutral operand, so the shape witness states the machine's own step with the stuck call occurring syntactically and hslot rewrites it afterwards. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_AFTER_LOAD, "The load with its lookup SUSPENDED. The lookup it suspends is ir_mem_lookup (ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv)) a -- a lookup INTO A STORE, which no head lemma resolves; ir_mem_lookup_update_hit does. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_STEP_STORE, "Shape witness: one machine step from ir_it3_smach IS the suspended store, by computation. Trace: fetch ir_it_func (ir_nat_eqb 0 0), block b5 (ir_block_find walks b0..b5), node at pc 1 = store ir_it_tresult %2 %29; ir_exec's store arm resolves %2 -> ptr a and %29 -> aggv spv through ir_it3_loc5 and ir_store_exec's ptr arm is ir_store_checked s a (aggv spv) (ir_mem_lookup mem2 a). Registered separately so a change to the store arm stops THIS reducing rather than silently changing what the seam is about. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_STORE_COMMITS, "With the lookup resolved to a LIVE cell holding any v0, the suspended store commits to ir_it3_amach by computation: ir_store_checked's some arm, ir_store_live at ir_slot_live (mk a v0 true) = true, ir_advance (ir_set_mem s (ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv))). The update stays neutral; v0 is overwritten and never read. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_STEP_BR, "The br b3 step over a NEUTRAL heap, by computation. Node at b5 pc 2 = br ir_d3 ir_nl0; ir_jump consults ir_cur_func (a hit at function 0 of ir_it_module), ir_block_find finds b3, ir_goto binds b3's empty parameter list and lands at pc zero. Nothing in the step reads memory and ir_goto's IRMachine.rec major is a CONSTRUCTOR with the heap only a field, so ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv) rides through untouched -- that is what makes the slot's position in memory irrelevant to this step. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_STEP_LOAD, "Shape witness: one step from ir_it3_bmach IS the suspended load. Node at b3 pc 0 = load ir_it_tresult %2 -> %5; the load arm's ir_load_view over ir_mod_encs ir_it_module = nil is the identity (ir_enc_find nil t = none, decided on the TABLE before the result is inspected, eval_ir_machine.rs:508), ir_load_eval resolves %2 -> ptr a and ir_load_at's ptr arm is ir_load_slot (ir_mem_lookup (ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv)) a) -- the lookup INTO the store this seam performed. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT3_LOAD_BINDS, "With the lookup resolved to the live cell now holding aggv spv, the suspended load binds %5 := aggv spv and advances to ir_it3_lmach by computation: ir_load_slot's some arm, ir_load_cell at live = true, ir_load_value's aggv arm returning the aggregate itself, ir_bind_result's value arm, ir_frame_bind at (ir_nl1 ir_d5). DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_TRANSPORT3_AT, "*** INFER_TYPE'S STORE / BR / LOAD, OVER THE TARGET ALONE, WITH THE RESULT SLOT ANYWHERE IN MEMORY. *** Three steps from the instant call 2 returns (b5 pc 1, %29 := aggv spv over the REAL b5 locals -- %4, %3, then %2 := ptr a under them, not ir_ite_loc's head rebinding) and the machine sits at b3 pc 1 ON the ret node, %5 := aggv spv bound, heap ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv), counter untouched -- for every p q, slot address a, spines sp and spv, dests ds, caller stack rest, prior slot content v0 and heap mem2 in which the slot is LIVE at a. Cost is derived: store (b5 node 1), br (b5 node 2), load (b3 node 0); the ret at b3 node 1 is deliberately NOT executed, so the conclusion is RUNNING and ir_it_seam3_ext transports it verbatim to IRModule.mk fs gs. The chain: ir_steps ir_d3 peels one step definitionally, the step is the named shape witness, the suspended lookup is rewritten by congruence -- hslot at the store, ir_mem_lookup_update_hit at the load, exactly where ir_it_transport_seg needed the head-of-memory assumption and no longer does -- and the resolved form computes to the next machine. ir_ite's hypothesis that the slot is the HEAD of memory was false for the real tick_heartbeat, which allocates; hslot replaces it and an allocating callee preserves it (ir_lzd_lookup_ext / MemExt). DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_D2_IS_D1_ADD_D1, "Literal arithmetic pin: ir_d2 IS Nat.add ir_d1 ir_d1 by computation. Nat.add recurses on its SECOND argument, so Nat.add ir_d1 ir_d1 -> succ (Nat.add ir_d1 ir_d0) -> succ ir_d1 -> succ (succ zero), which is ir_d2's normal form. Lets a cost written Nat.add X ir_d2 be identified with the literal ir_d2 segment if the elaborator's unifier refuses to do it silently. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_D4_IS_D1_ADD_D3, "Literal arithmetic pin: ir_d4 IS Nat.add ir_d1 ir_d3 by computation -- three iota steps on the second argument then Nat.add ir_d1 zero = ir_d1, giving succ^4 zero, which is what ir_d4 delta-unfolds to. This is the identification BOTH ir_d4 segments rest on: the THREE steps run first and the ONE step last, because ir_steps_add m b a c splits Nat.add b a with a executed first. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_STEPS1_IS_STEP, "One step of the iterator on a running configuration IS ir_step, by computation: ir_steps unfolds to ir_drive_v1, Nat.rec on ir_d1 = succ ir_d0 takes the succ minor, the halted test on running s is Bool.false so Bool.rec's FIRST minor ih (step c0) fires, and ih at zero is the identity. The same definitional fact ir_stk_activation relies on at its last Eq.trans leg; pinned here by name so a failure in the ir_steps-form twins is attributable to this reduction. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_STEPS4_SPLIT, "The peel BOTH four-step segments use: four steps are three steps FOLLOWED BY one step. ir_steps_add m ir_d1 ir_d3 c has type ir_steps (Nat.add ir_d1 ir_d3) m c = ir_steps ir_d1 m (ir_steps ir_d3 m c); the declared type spells the fuel as the literal ir_d4, definitionally that sum (ir_d4_is_d1_add_d3). Generic in m and c, so it serves the dispatch segment (3 seam steps then the call-2 push) and the transport segment (store/br/load then the ret) unchanged. Register AFTER ir_d4_is_d1_add_d3 so that, if the elaborator refuses the silent identification here, the named pin beside it says whether the arithmetic or the split is what failed. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_HF, "The ret step's FUNCTION premise, in exactly the spelling ir_stk_ret_step (S4) takes it: h0 restated with the module and frame projections syntactic. ir_mod_funcs (IRModule.mk fs gs) is fs and ir_frame_func (IRFrame.mk ir_d0 ..) is ir_d0 by one iota each, so the body is h0 itself and the only defeq is at this declaration's boundary -- which keeps every application in ir_it_ag_ret_loc purely syntactic. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_HB, "The ret step's BLOCK premise: block ir_d3 of the minted ir_it_func is ir_it_b3, by computation. ir_block_find walks b0 (ir_nat_eqb ir_d0 ir_d3 = false via ir_nat_iszero), b1 (ir_nat_sub_eqb ir_d0 ir_d2 = false), b2 (ir_nat_sub_eqb ir_d1 ir_d2 = false) and hits b3 (ir_nat_sub_eqb ir_d2 ir_d2 = true) -- four closed-literal comparisons, the same walk ir_it_transport_seg already performs. The locals tail loc is abstract because nothing here reads it. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_HN, "The ret step's NODE premise: node 1 of ir_it_b3 is ret %5, by computation. ir_block_nodes ir_it_b3 is ir_bd2 (load -> %5) (ret [%5]); ir_nodes_get at pc ir_d1 = succ ir_d0 skips the load and returns the second node, which is ir_nd (IRInst.ret (ir_nl1 ir_d5)) = IRNode.mk (IRInst.ret (ir_nl1 ir_d5)) ir_nl0 -- so the rs a ret node declares is ir_nl0 (ir_nd is the no-result node builder), which is the rs ir_it_ag_ret_loc passes to ir_stk_ret_step. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_DESTS, "The b3 frame's return destinations are the ds ir_push installed, by one iota on IRFrame.mk. Named so the identification of ir_stk_ret_step's ir_frame_dests f with the theorem's own ds is a pinned fact rather than a silent unfolding. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_RESOLVE, "Resolving [%5] in the b3 frame yields [aggv spv], by computation: ir_resolve conses ir_getd s ir_d5 = ir_frames_get (cons F rest) ir_d5 = ir_frame_get F ir_d5 = ir_opt_value (ir_binding_lookup (cons (%5 := aggv spv) loc) ir_d5), and that lookup is a HEAD HIT (ir_nat_eqb ir_d5 ir_d5 -> ir_nat_sub_eqb ir_d4 ir_d4 = true), so the abstract tail loc is never walked; the resolved tail is IRList.rec on ir_nl0, i.e. ir_vl1's tail. This is why the lemma can quantify the rest of the locals away: the ret reads exactly one binding and it sits at the head, where ir_bind put it. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_LOC, "*** THE FINAL RET STEP OF infer_type AT AN ABSTRACT MODULE. *** From the b3 frame at pc 1 with %5 bound to aggv spv at the head of its locals, over ANY tail loc, ANY caller stack rest, ANY heap memF and counter naF, one ir_step at IRModule.mk fs gs is ir_ret_to ds rest memF naF [aggv spv] -- given only h0. It is ir_stk_ret_step (S4) applied with fn := ir_it_func, b := ir_it_b3, ids := ir_nl1 ir_d5, rs := ir_nl0 and the three premises supplied by their named pins, so every argument is syntactic; the one definitional identification is at the declared type, where S4's ir_ret_to (ir_frame_dests f) rest memF naF (ir_resolve s ids) computes to the stated form (ir_it_ag_ret_dests and ir_it_ag_ret_resolve pin each half). No callee, no heap shape, no module contents beyond h0. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET, "ir_it_ag_ret_loc at the transport seam's ACTUAL output frame, locals explicit in p q na sp spv -- the DERIVATION RECORD for the seven-binding list, head to entry: %5 := aggv spv (b3's load; ir_frame_bind conses at the HEAD and bumps pc from ir_frame_goto's Nat.zero to ir_d1); %29 := aggv spv (hc2's ir_ret_to through ir_frame_set_many); %4 := int_ ir_d0 and %3 := ir_it_hb_answer sp (the dispatch seam's two bindings, exactly ir_it_dispatch_end's); %2 := ptr_ na (b0's alloca binds IRScalar.ptr_ at the counter of that moment, the initial na); then the entry locals computed to %0 := ptr_ p, %1 := ptr_ q. Block ir_d3 from the br's ir_frame_goto. That list is ir_it3_loc5 with %5 consed on, by two deltas. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_RET_STEPS1, "The SPLICE-READY form of the ret step: the same fact through the iterator and at the transport seam's own output spelling ir_it3_lmach, which is what the ir_d4 = ir_d3 + ir_d1 split of the transport segment hands the assembly. The body is ir_it_ag_ret_loc at loc := ir_it3_loc5 p q a sp spv, memF := ir_mem_update mem2 a (aggv spv), naF := na2 -- a pure application; the declared type differs from the body's type by exactly two reductions, the ir_steps peel ir_it_ag_steps1_is_step pins and one delta of ir_it3_lmach. Registered at this spelling rather than at the explicit seven-binding list so the assembly's Eq.trans leg is SYNTACTIC. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_HC2_LANDS_ON_SMACH, "*** THE ONE SPLICE THAT WOULD OTHERWISE BE UNNAMED (audit defect 2). *** What hc2 delivers IS where the transport seam starts, by computation, at the CONCRETE locals the assembly is at. Left side: ir_ret_to with dests [29] into the advanced b5 caller frame over rest, at mem2/na2, returning [aggv spv]. Right side: IRConfig.running (ir_it3_smach p q na sp spv ds rest mem2 na2). The reduction is ir_ret_to's cons arm, ir_frame_set_many's match (pc NOT advanced -- the push already advanced it), ir_bind_params [29] [aggv spv] LOC = cons (%29, aggv spv) LOC, and two deltas on ir_it3_loc5 / ir_it3_loc0. Every other seam boundary in this stage is pinned by its own declaration; before this one existed the hc2-to-transport boundary was discharged only inside whatever Eq.trans the assembly wrote, so a refusal there was unattributable. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ACTIVATION, "*** THE A4-SHAPED ACTIVATION FOR TypeChecker::infer_type, OVER AN ABSTRACT MODULE, WITH ITS TWO CALLEES AS CONTRACTS. *** For every fs and gs in which function 0 is the MINTED ir_it_func (h0), function 1 is some g1 (h1) and function 2 is some g2 (h2); for every heap mem, counter na, entry pointers p q, dests ds and caller stack rest; given hc1 (tick_heartbeat returns ir_it_hb_answer sp in c1 steps, into EVERY caller frame list), hc2 (infer_type_fast returns aggv spv in c2 steps, likewise) and hslot (the Result slot at the entry counter na is LIVE in the heap the inference leaves behind) -- infer_type runs from its entry configuration to ir_ret_to ds rest (ir_mem_update mem2 na (aggv spv)) na2 [aggv spv] in EXACTLY Nat.add (Nat.add (Nat.add (Nat.add ir_d4 c2) ir_d4) c1) ir_d2 steps. NO AUTHORED MODEL APPEARS: g1 and g2 are quantified IRFuncs constrained only by the contracts, the module is IRModule.mk fs gs, and heap, counter, caller stack and payload are free -- the difference from ir_itd, which proves the same transport by RUNNING two hand-written callee models at a pinned heap. THE COST IS DERIVED and its right-nesting is load-bearing because Nat.add recurses on its SECOND argument, so ir_steps_add m b a c executes a FIRST: 2 (b0 alloca, b0 call-1 push), c1, 4 (br / extractfield / switch then the call-2 push), c2, 4 (store / br / load then the ret). At c1 = c2 = 2 -- ir_itd's two-node models -- this is 14, which is what ir_itd_transports_the_inference_result measured. EVERY SPLICE IS NAMED: the prologue's output IS hc1's premise at d := ir_nl1 ir_d3; hc1's output IS ir_it_dispatch_seg's start; the seam's output IS the machine ir_it_ag_call2 steps from; that push's output IS hc2's premise at d := ir_nl1 ir_d29; hc2's output IS ir_it3_smach (ir_it_ag_hc2_lands_on_smach); the transport's output IS the frame ir_it_ag_ret_loc returns from. The two CONCRETE-module seams cross to the abstract module through ir_it_seam3_ext, i.e. ir_mext_run under h0 alone. WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: hc1 and hc2 are PREMISES, not theorems. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_INIT, "What ir_init builds at an ABSTRACT module, given h0 alone -- the abstract-module twin of ir_it_init_is_mach0, which is Eq.refl only because ir_it_module is concrete. ir_init's own IROption.rec is stuck at the neutral ir_func_find fs ir_d0, so one suspended-lookup Eq.subst resolves it and everything then computes: ir_func_id ir_it_func and ir_func_entry ir_it_func are ir_d0, ir_func_params ir_it_func is ir_nl2 ir_d0 ir_d1, the outermost frame gets NO return destinations (IRList.nil Nat) so its ret halts the machine, and the heap is ir_mem_concat (ir_globals_mem gs) mem0 -- left folded, because at an abstract gs it is neutral and nothing in this run inspects it. That neutral heap is exactly the mem the activation is instantiated at. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_CORRECT, "*** METATHEORY, NOT A4 (decision memo D5(d); section 11): an assume-guarantee statement over an ABSTRACT module whose function 0 is the ir_it_func minted from the 2026-09-16 sidecar dump. That minted body is NOT the object that ships today (scripts/crystal_link4_join.py reads it RED against the current extraction: the Err arm then havocked the payload that is now threaded), and link 4 soundness targets the env-indexed TypingCtxConvIn family, not this. Never cite it as A4 for the deployed infer_type. *** ir_eval fuel (IRModule.mk fs gs) 0 [ptr p, ptr q] mem0 na = IROutcome.ret [aggv spv], for EVERY module whose function 0 is the minted ir_it_func and whose functions 1 and 2 satisfy the two callee contracts, at every caller heap mem0 and counter na, with enough fuel. It is ir_it_ag_activation at ds := nil and rest := nil -- where ir_ret_to's IRList.rec takes its nil minor and HALTS with IROutcome.ret -- composed exactly as ir_lzb_correct composes ir_lzb_activation: ir_it_ag_init resolves ir_init's own suspended lookup under h0, ir_run_of_steps turns the iterator into the runner, and ir_run_le_ret weakens the exact cost to any Le-larger fuel. THE RESIDUAL IS THE TWO CONTRACTS AND IS NOT DISCHARGED HERE. hc2 (infer_type_fast) is discharge-able in principle -- its closure is 113 functions / 7379 instructions, registrable at about 5 percent of the spec, and ir_stk_activation plus ir_mext_run are the two rules that carry a standalone run of it into this statement. hc1 (tick_heartbeat, 313 functions / 55122 instructions) is not, and remains an ASSUMPTION about a profiler whose effect is orthogonal to the type checker's answer; hslot is its heap half, and an allocating heartbeat preserves it through ir_lzd_lookup_ext / MemExt. No authored MODEL appears in the statement, which is the difference from ir_itd. CENSUS NOTE FOR THE INTEGRATOR: this name starts with ir_it_ and contains correct, so it trips tests/eval_ir_its_census.rs the_designated_target_is_registered_and_halts_at_its_first_callee (lines 126-133), whose assertion refuses an A4-shaped ir_it_ name. That guard must be amended deliberately -- admitting a correct name only when both contract premises are visible in its statement -- not deleted. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_FS, "ir_it_ag_itd_fs: the function table ir_itd_module carries, NAMED rather than transcribed -- the minted target at id 0, the authored heartbeat at id 1, the authored inference model at id 2. It is factored out only so the activation's `fs` binder can be instantiated with a term for which `IRModule.mk fs (IRList.nil IRGlobal)` is DEFINITIONALLY ir_itd_module (pinned beside it by ir_it_ag_itd_module_is), which is what lets the witness's conclusion be a statement about ir_itd_module and not about a lookalike. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_MODULE_IS, "ir_it_ag_itd_module_is: the module the assume-guarantee theorem is instantiated at IS ir_itd_module, by computation. Registered as its own declaration rather than left to a defeq check inside a 25-argument application, so that if the split into `fs`/`gs` ever stops agreeing with ir_itd_module the failure names THIS line instead of surfacing as an unexplained mismatch in the witness. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_HBSP, "ir_it_ag_itd_hbsp: the heartbeat model's answer SPINE -- the two undef payload slots that sit after the discriminant. This is the value the activation's universally-quantified `sp : IRScalar` takes at ir_itd_module, and it is DERIVED rather than chosen: ir_itb_hb_b0's constant is IRConst.aggv (vcons (int_ 0) (vcons undef (vcons undef vnil))), ir_const_agg_eval yields IRScalar.aggv (ir_const_value <spine>) because ir_ty_is_agg (IRTy.struct_ 2) is true, and ir_const_value maps vcons/vnil/int_/undef_ constructor-for-constructor -- so the machine's answer is ir_it_hb_answer at exactly this spine and at no other. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_SPV, "ir_it_ag_itd_spv: the payload spine the inference model hands back, as an IRScalar -- the value the activation's `spv` takes at ir_itd_module. It is derived through ir_const_value from ir_itd_cval's own spine, so the two chains cite ONE spelling and cannot drift. spc stays universally quantified: ir_const_value spc is stuck at the neutral spc, but identically on both sides of every equation below, which is exactly why ir_itd could quantify the payload in the first place. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_ANSWER_IS_AGGV, "ir_it_ag_itd_answer_is_aggv: the value ir_itd's own theorem returns IS the `IRScalar.aggv spv` shape the assume-guarantee contract demands, with spv = ir_it_ag_itd_spv. This is the bridge that makes the two routes comparable at all -- hc2's right-hand side is head-constructor-constrained (ir_load_value matches on the scalar and is stuck at a neutral one), and this pins that ir_itd_answer meets that constraint for EVERY payload spine rather than for a witness. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_HB_BINDS_THE_ANSWER, "ir_it_ag_itd_hb_binds_the_answer: ONE step of the heartbeat model binds %1 to ir_it_hb_answer ir_it_ag_itd_hbsp. Registered as a separate, smaller failure locus for hc1 below: this half is about the CONST node -- whether the spine instantiation is the right one -- while the second step is about the RET node and the frame-generic return. A single Eq.refl over both would make those two indistinguishable on a refusal. The frame's fnid/block are written as the literals ir_d1/ir_d0 rather than as ir_func_id/ir_func_entry, which is the IRFunc.rec iota the checker performs; the pc advance to ir_d1 is ir_frame_bind's own Nat.succ. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_FAST_BINDS_THE_PAYLOAD, "ir_it_ag_itd_fast_binds_the_payload: ONE step of the inference model binds %2 to IRScalar.aggv (ir_it_ag_itd_spv spc), for EVERY payload spine spc. The hc2 companion of the previous declaration and the same reason for existing. It is also where the abstract spine is seen not to block: the const arm goes through ir_const_agg_eval, whose ir_ty_is_agg test reads the declared TYPE (IRTy.struct_ 2) and never the spine, so spc is carried opaquely rather than forced. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_HC1_AT_ITD, "*** THE FIRST CALLEE CONTRACT, DISCHARGED BY COMPUTATION AT A CONCRETE MODULE. *** The activation's hc1 premise, in exactly its frame-generic `forall (d) (r)` form, proved at ir_itd_module's own fs/gs with g1 = ir_itb_hb. TWO steps, which is derived from the body and not guessed: ir_itb_hb_b0 is ir_bd2 -- a const node and a ret node -- so the cost is two, and 2 + c1 + 4 + c2 + 4 with c1 = c2 = 2 lands on the FOURTEEN ir_itd's own cost pin fixes (fuel_out at 13, ret at 14). \\n\\nThe heap and the counter stay quantified because the model performs no alloca, store or load: ir_bind and ir_ret_vals rebuild the machine through IRMachine.rec and carry mem/na opaquely. d and r stay quantified because ir_ret_to is an IRList.rec on r, stuck at a neutral r IDENTICALLY on both sides -- which is what makes one Eq.refl serve every caller frame, and is the property the activation actually consumes when it applies hc1 under the target's own suspended frame. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_HC2_AT_ITD, "*** THE SECOND CALLEE CONTRACT, DISCHARGED BY COMPUTATION AT A CONCRETE MODULE. *** The activation's hc2 premise at g2 = ir_itd_fast spc, same shape and same two-step cost -- ir_itd_fast_b0 is also ir_bd2, a const node and a ret node. The returned value is IRScalar.aggv (ir_it_ag_itd_spv spc), which is the head-constructor form hc2 demands, for EVERY payload spine spc. \\n\\nThe output heap is the INPUT heap unchanged, which is the fact that lets the activation's mem2/na2 be instantiated to the same terms as mem1/na1 and is why hslot below can still see the alloca's undef: the store into the Result slot is the caller's node, executed four steps LATER, not the callee's. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_H0_AT_ITD, "ir_it_ag_h0_at_itd: the target resolves at index 0, by computation -- ir_func_find compares ir_func_id against the key with ir_nat_eqb, and at a concrete three-element table over concrete literal ids every comparison decides. An Eq.refl, as the task's item 2 anticipated. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_H1_AT_ITD, "ir_it_ag_h1_at_itd: the heartbeat model resolves at index 1 -- one false ir_nat_eqb and then a hit. Eq.refl. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_H2_AT_ITD, "ir_it_ag_h2_at_itd: the inference model resolves at index 2, for every spc -- ir_func_find's IRFunc.rec reads only the id field, so the quantified payload never obstructs the lookup. Eq.refl. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_HSLOT_AT_ITD, "ir_it_ag_hslot_at_itd: the Result slot is live and still holds the alloca's undef when the inference call returns -- so the activation's v0 is IRScalar.undef_. This IS an Eq.refl, and only because the address is the CONCRETE ir_d7 that ir_itd runs at: ir_mem_lookup's head test is ir_nat_eqb ir_d7 ir_d7, which decides, where at an abstract counter it is stuck at a neutral operand and the same fact needs ir_mem_lookup_head and an Eq.subst (the split eval_ir_slot_lemmas.rs and ir_it_transport_seg both live with). The heap TAIL stays quantified, because a head hit never walks it. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_ITD_COST_IS_FOURTEEN, "ir_it_ag_itd_cost_is_fourteen: the activation's cost expression, at the two callee costs this module actually has, IS fourteen. Registered as its own declaration because it is the arithmetic the whole cross-check turns on: 2 (alloca, call 1) + 2 (c1) + 4 (br, extractfield, switch, call 2) + 2 (c2) + 4 (store, br, load, ret). That is the same fourteen ir_itd_transports_the_inference_result runs to and one more than ir_itd_is_still_running_at_thirteen, so the assume-guarantee decomposition and the direct run agree on the cost and not merely on the answer. Same Nat.add-on-numerals mechanism as ir_d2_is_d1_add_d1. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_WITNESS_AT_COST_EXPR, "*** THE NON-VACUITY WITNESS: ALL SIX PREMISES OF ir_it_ag_activation, SIMULTANEOUSLY SATISFIED, AT A CONCRETE MODULE. *** The assume-guarantee theorem has two universally-quantified callee contracts among its hypotheses; nothing registered previously showed they could hold TOGETHER, so nothing ruled out a vacuously-true statement -- the shape the vacuity firewall exists to refuse. This is that application: h0/h1/h2 and hslot are Eq.refl lookups, hc1 and hc2 are two-step computations over the module's own authored models, and what comes out is a CLOSED equation about ir_steps over ir_itd_module. \\n\\nds and rest are left ABSTRACT, so the witness is frame-generic exactly as the theorem is -- it does not buy satisfiability by collapsing to one caller. The cost is stated as the theorem's own expression rather than as a numeral, so this declaration's declared type is its inferred type verbatim and nothing here depends on numeral arithmetic; ir_it_ag_witness reduces it to the literal fourteen through ir_it_ag_itd_cost_is_fourteen. \\n\\nWhat it does NOT establish: the theorem is not made stronger, and ir_itd's two residuals are untouched -- both callees are still authored models, so this witnesses SATISFIABILITY of the contracts, never that the real tick_heartbeat or infer_type_fast meet them. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_WITNESS, "*** THE WITNESS AT THE LITERAL COST, OVER ir_itd_module BY NAME. *** The same fact as ir_it_ag_witness_at_cost_expr with the assume-guarantee cost expression REWRITTEN to fourteen through ir_it_ag_itd_cost_is_fourteen, rather than left to a defeq check inside a 25-argument application -- so the arithmetic is a step a reader can see and a refusal can name. The statement now reads: fourteen steps of ir_itd_module from infer_type's entry configuration, at the empty heap and counter seven, under ANY caller destinations ds and ANY caller stack rest, reach the caller with the Result slot holding the transported aggregate and the payload returned. \\n\\nIt keeps the heap effect visible, which the outcome-level form below discards: the slot at address 7 has gone from the alloca's undef to IRScalar.aggv (ir_it_ag_itd_spv spc), and that is the memory round-trip ir_itd's docs describe, here as the conclusion of an assume-guarantee argument rather than of a whole-module run. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_WITNESS_EVAL, "ir_it_ag_witness_eval: the same witness carried through ir_it_ag_correct to the ir_eval form -- ir_init, ir_run_of_steps and ir_run_le_ret, at ds = rest = nil, with the fuel bound discharged by Le.refl at the exact cost. This is the form that can be compared with ir_itd's independently-proved theorem, which is the next declaration. \\n\\nThe heap arguments are spelled ir_mem_concat (ir_globals_mem (IRList.nil IRGlobal)) ir_mem0 rather than ir_mem0 ON PURPOSE: that is the literal form ir_it_ag_correct's own premises take once gs and mem0 are instantiated, so every hypothesis matches the expected type SYNTACTICALLY and no reduction of the globals prologue is asked of the checker in a hypothesis position. The reduction is real (an empty global table materialises no cells) and is left to the one place it is load-bearing, the conclusion. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_WITNESS_AGREES, "*** THE INSTANTIATION IS CHECKED AGAINST AN INDEPENDENTLY-PROVED FACT, NOT AGAINST ITSELF. *** The answer the assume-guarantee route produces equals the answer ir_itd's direct fourteen-step run produces, for every payload spine spc and both pointer arguments -- and the proof TERM is what carries that content: it composes ir_it_ag_witness_eval with ir_itd_transports_the_inference_result through the ir_eval term they share, so the two routes are joined at a point each proves about independently rather than the agreement being asserted. \\n\\nStated honestly: at a concrete module this equation is also reachable by computation, so the statement is not what makes the check non-trivial -- the derivation is. The falsifiable content sits one level down, in ir_it_ag_hc1_at_itd and ir_it_ag_hc2_at_itd (a wrong step count refuses to typecheck at all) and in ir_it_ag_itd_cost_is_fourteen (a wrong pair of callee costs cannot sum to the fourteen ir_itd's own cost pin fixes). DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
    (SRC_IR_IT_AG_WITNESS_COST_IS_TIGHT, "ir_it_ag_witness_cost_is_tight: the assume-guarantee cost MINUS ONE is not enough -- at that fuel the machine is still running. Registered so the witness's fourteen is pinned as the EXACT cost of the decomposition rather than as an over-approximation that happens to work, and it is pinned by ir_itd's own lower half, which was measured on the direct run and knows nothing about the activation. Together with ir_it_ag_itd_cost_is_fourteen this closes the cost from both sides: the assume-guarantee expression evaluates to fourteen, the run needs fourteen, and thirteen does not do it. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps."),
];

impl Specification {
    /// The assume-guarantee activation. MUST follow `add_eval_ir_ite` (the two
    /// seams), `add_eval_ir_stack_theorems` (S3/S5 and `ir_mext_run`) and
    /// `add_eval_ir_lzd_fresh` (`ir_bool_false_ne_true`).
    pub(super) fn add_eval_ir_itf(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        for (src, why) in DECLS {
            self.add_recursive_def(src, why)?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}
